{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions","id":285045,"title":"New Scion ST, asking questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-17T09:40:23-07:00","id":285045,"title":"New Scion ST, asking questions","content":"Hey there, OP forums!<br /> My group is going to try out Scion 1st editon and I have a few questions I hope you could help me with:<br /> <br /> Just how &quot;open&quot; is the secret of supernatural and divine creatures? Some of the things Scions can do and some of the creatures they fight just aren't subtle, and I wonder how their existance isn't common knowledge, at least without some sort of omnipresent supernatural &quot;camoflauge&quot;, like the Mist in PJO. I haven't found a satisfactory anwer in the book.<br /> <br /> How involved should be a Scion's divine parents with their children? I can guess that the answer is &quot;it varies&quot;, but if someone could make some examples for me, I'd really like it.<br /> <br /> As for mechanics, while I've played others WW/Onyx Path games, Scion is new to me, so I was wondering if it had any traps or problems beyond what's usual for the Storyteller System and it's variants, both for players and me, the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T12:53:11-07:00","id":285216,"title":"","content":"The default assumption is that Scions and Titanspawn are really just entering the world. There hasn't been time for a lot of big things to happen, so the world is pretty unaware. However there <i>is</i> no &quot;Mist&quot;, no Delirium and no Masquerade. So if a Scion goes running around New York tossing cars around and fighting Fire Giants, it'll make the headlines. The world will have to decide what to believe. It really is entirely up to each game how the world deals with those revelations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T17:23:43-07:00","id":285549,"title":"","content":"Is that so? Even though rereading the introduction now it seems actually quite obvious, for some reason I had always assumed that Scion had always been part of the World for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-17T23:26:10-07:00","id":285732,"title":"","content":"Nawp. They're supposed to be quite the revolutionary change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T04:08:58-07:00","id":285807,"title":"","content":"But I thout there had been scions and titanspawns fighting in both World Wars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T07:33:42-07:00","id":285889,"title":"","content":"The major setting change is the escape of the Titans and their siege of the God Realms of the Pantheons in the Overworld. At that point it can be expected that Titanspawn, able to enter the world and act in greater numbers and power than ever before, can &quot;go loud&quot; and stop hiding. Prior to the break out of the Titans its implied if not outright stated that Scions and Titanspawn tread carefully because each attracts the attention of the other if they are too blatant. Scions also tend to get visited for a purpose and many never actually find out they are the children of gods. They are left ignorant unless circumstances dictate their parent or another relative needs an agent on Earth who won't attract as much attention as acting directly. Except for things like World Wars, the Gods tend to have a gentlebeing's agreement not to meddle too much or descend upon the Earth in their full glory.<br /> <br /> Scions and Titanspawn have always been in the world and even some famous individuals were Scions. However due to the risk of becoming Fate Bound and attracting unwanted attention (there's always a bigger fish) Scions and Titanspawn rarely blatantly reveal themselves to large numbers of witnesses. When they do it seems to become the subject of folklore but it can blow back on the divine beings and saddle them with unwanted responsibilities, prophecies and destinies. Fate seems to be the force that nudges anything with a legend score to keep their actions covert unless they want Fate to write ever more interesting destinies for them. Generally speaking, the more epic the deeds of the legendary being, the more Fate throws at them until they either persevere or die. So the more legendary the deeds, the more Fate Binding can sink its claws in.<br /> <br /> My guess is that because regular humans generally perceive titan spawns to be normal(ish) people or objects even when they are hideous monsters this also represents a reflexive tendency to rationalize whatever they see with their understanding of the world. So memories of throwing a car might be interpreted as a spectacular car crash either immediately or over time. Scion tends to leave a lot of open spaces for the storyteller to decide to what degree mortals can perceive what's really going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1881,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","user":"The Cowardly Scion","date":".  Additions and clarifications 10-18-2014, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T09:08:34-07:00","id":285961,"title":"","content":"As for how involved the parent is, as unsatisfying as it may be of an answer, I would have to say that it depends on the parent. Scions of the more tiered, formal and/or bureaucratic pantheons like the Celestial Bureaucracy and the Amatsukami may (possibly) get an initial Visit from their parent and then only see them (or perhaps only see their intermediaries) when there are new orders for them to carry out. The more family oriented pantheons like the Loa or the Tuatha D\u00e9 Danann may spend more time with 'the kids', both socially and to see how they're doing.<br /> <br /> Of course your experiences may vary. Someone you might expect to be aloof and distant like Hel might spend all the time she can with a Scion micro-managing him/her or just because she has so few Scion children of her own that she wants to see them as much as she can and that there's something about 'this one' that appeals to her.<br /> <br /> And, also, there is the fact that there is a war on and while some godly parents may want to spend all the time in the world with their kid (either because they like the kid or they want to micro-manage what they're doing) between their dread and dislike of being Fatebound and the fact that they're under siege it may simply not be possible to do more than snatch the occasional quick visit away. Gods who travel as part of their thing may be able to snatch more time as they drop in between duties but really, how much time a given god can (or wants to) get away is up to what's going on and their general nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-18T11:51:30-07:00","id":286092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=285807#post285807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I thout there had been scions and titanspawns fighting in both World Wars?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The WWII supplement is a dividing, dangerous topic around here. Some love it and include it as actual canon in their games. Others wished it had never seen the light of day. WWII is just a setting hack to open up the Titan War inside what's already a dangerous war itself. Issues with the supplement aside, you can either take it or leave it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T03:16:00-07:00","id":286551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=286092#post286092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The WWII supplement is a dividing, dangerous topic around here. Some love it and include it as actual canon in their games. Others wished it had never seen the light of day. WWII is just a setting hack to open up the Titan War inside what's already a dangerous war itself. Issues with the supplement aside, you can either take it or leave it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies, I had no idea it was a hot subject. Still, if can ignore it, all the better for my game, all things considered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 10-19-2014, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-21T17:20:42-07:00","id":289118,"title":"","content":"So, as I prepare for the game, I think I'm going to keep using this to post my thoughts. Please, comment and make suggestions if you feel like it, I would greatly appreciate it.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, my players have brought to me their character concepts, and a few even have sheets! And names! And backstories!<br /> <br /> Anywya, our Band looks to be comprised of:<br /> Max &quot;The Hammer&quot; Thurman, Scion of Thor, a former boxers who quit after he was asked to (and threatened) throw a match. He's become a bouncer since then, acting sometimes as a vigilante for a while before his Visitation came;<br /> <br /> Christopher Ventura, Scion of Hades, a killer for hire with his own &quot;code&quot;. He's a bit neurotic in his mannerism, clearly having OCD. His Visitation came when his own father hired him to &quot;kill&quot; what was an escapee from his realm, as test, before revealing himself.<br /> <br /> Ricardo Morales, Scion of Uhizilopochtli, a former Army Sergeant, now works as private security. The one with the more solid backstory, he crossed over the Mexico border with his mother when very young, and joined the Army once of age to gain citizenship. He was however dishonorably discharged after his bloodthirtyness led his to gun down what he believed to be terrorists while in Iraq, disobeying orders. After his return home and the death of his mother, he rerurned to his hometown to see if he had any other blood relatives, leading to his Visitation.<br /> <br /> The last two are still nameless, two women, respectively a professional thief Scion of Bast (many Catwoman jokes were had), and a magician and illusionist Scion of Loki.<br /> <br /> I'm still thinking on what to do when it comes to the actual plot of my game. I kinda want to have the first story be the actual first meeting and adventure as a group for the PCs, unlike handwaving it away like we always do.<br /> I'm a bit stumped at the moment however. I'm looking back to my old mythology books to try and get inspiration, but I haven't really found anything that I like as the focus for the story. The example story in the book isn't really to my liking, even though I still like Vegas as the setting for it.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any thoughts on the PC's? Suggestions or ideas from your own games would be incredibly appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T00:49:00-07:00","id":289323,"title":"","content":"There is one thing you can do which will make your life much easier. Ask the players to sit down (or chat online) with each other, and figure out between themselves how they all know each other / possibly have done jobs together before / have become friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T02:56:46-07:00","id":289389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289323#post289323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is one thing you can do which will make your life much easier. Ask the players to sit down (or chat online) with each other, and figure out between themselves how they all know each other / possibly have done jobs together before / have become friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's surprising how rarely that actually happens in our games. For some reason we always place the enterety of the burden of the plot on our ST/GM (usually me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T04:27:59-07:00","id":289438,"title":"","content":"On another subject, in your experience, how useful actually are boons? Some of my players were complaining that compared to most Knacks, some 1 and 2 dot boons are useless and/or boring at first glance?<br /> Did you find this to be true in game as well? Any solutions, or resources to help with this, if it's actually a problem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T04:31:15-07:00","id":289440,"title":"","content":"Also, as with many other WoD games, you might want to ask your players about the subjects they consider taboo. It's a game about ancient mythology, and sometimes it was not pretty. There's a lot a myths that features rape, slavery, bestiality, sometimes even pedophilia...<br /> Also, with the right powers, it's super easy for Scions to brainwash people, which can make some players uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I may sound a bit prudish, but clearly establishing which subjects are okay to use and which ones aren't helps a lot in having a healthy table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T05:07:13-07:00","id":289446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289440#post289440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as with many other WoD games, you might want to ask your players about the subjects they consider taboo. It's a game about ancient mythology, and sometimes it was not pretty. There's a lot a myths that features rape, slavery, bestiality, sometimes even pedophilia...<br /> Also, with the right powers, it's super easy for Scions to brainwash people, which can make some players uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I may sound a bit prudish, but clearly establishing which subjects are okay to use and which ones aren't helps a lot in having a healthy table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not really worried about offending any of my players, mostly because we've all been friends for years before we even started gaming togheter, and I know them all well enough to know what I can and can't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T08:54:09-07:00","id":289630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289438#post289438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On another subject, in your experience, how useful actually are boons? Some of my players were complaining that compared to most Knacks, some 1 and 2 dot boons are useless and/or boring at first glance?<br /> Did you find this to be true in game as well? Any solutions, or resources to help with this, if it's actually a problem?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is a concern. It has no solution, aside from re-writing the game. Epics are more useful, more powerful, provide more benefit and generally are cooler. The best Hero Boons are the Immunity Boons, Animal Aspect at Animal 3, and the ability to fly at Sky 2. Aside from those, you're going to notice that Boons just kinda suck. But don't worry, the entire Scion system is terrible, so it'll just fit in fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T09:59:38-07:00","id":289673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289118#post289118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still thinking on what to do when it comes to the actual plot of my game. I kinda want to have the first story be the actual first meeting and adventure as a group for the PCs, unlike handwaving it away like we always do.<br /> I'm a bit stumped at the moment however. I'm looking back to my old mythology books to try and get inspiration, but I haven't really found anything that I like as the focus for the story. The example story in the book isn't really to my liking, even though I still like Vegas as the setting for it.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have any thoughts on the PC's? Suggestions or ideas from your own games would be incredibly appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can try to go the wrote where there is some chain of previous relation and interaction. It can work. It usually doesn't provide the impetus for a group to STAY together which is a very important and neglected part of building a group. Unless they are siblings, lovers, childhood friends, brothers/sisters-in-arms, etc. you are going to have to fall back on something that might be as arbitrary as handwaving them all into group. Arbitrary in the sense of - FATE forces you to stay together, one/some/all of the divine parents DEMAND the group to stay a group, etc. Which can really effectively beat down on some characters who have concepts that would lead them away from the group. You can offset this by getting the players on board with making their decisions bend towards solidarity to the band when faced with a choice. But overall, 'we all know each other' or 'i know him and he knows her and that guy is his SO and her brother' might work, but it might not.<br /> <br /> Particularly since you have really solid character concepts in place already, you are going to need them to retool their histories or go another way. Wouldn't the cat burglar want to burgle? What if the OCD assassin doesn't want that b/c he feels compelled to find his next target? And the bouncer might want to stay near the bar, figuring that a job which provides cash for food is worth keeping.... etc. etc. There definitely needs to be something to glue them all together. Or plan in lots of downtime for them to pursue their own objectives.<br /> <br /> Hmmm..... ways that I have started off a group with the hope they stay together:<br /> <br /> 1st game: a 'strange attractor' - something happens that all the characters have some independent reason to get involved in - rumors of zombies lead to the forensic scientist, the tabloid reporter and biker who seems to have lost a buddy. Trick was to keep them acting together until the group got settled as a functioning unit by having the initial plot be big enough to keep the arc going whenever they needed a push. Others started regarding them as a group before they thought of themselves that way and began to act ON them as a team... That promoted some cohesion.<br /> <br /> 2nd game: (Probably the best overall game) they started off in a hospital-prison hooked up to IVs with some clear shining fluid in it and amnesia that went back to before their Visitations. (They did stumble across their Relics and know that they were 'important' somehow... I was not THAT cruel). So it started with a Great Escape feel, then a Wilderness Trek, then trying to recover their memories and figure out what had been done to them, all while dodging the people who captured them then hunting them down....<br /> <br /> 3rd game: The Venn diagrams of what their parents wanted and what their enemies wanted overlapped (thanks Fate!) then all ended up in a highway reststop when an unseasonal blizzard hit The rest stop restaraunt workers were possessed by wendigo and had adulterated the hamburgers with human flesh... all the mortals started becoming cannibal monsters.... the master of the wendigo got away, but left a clue as to where they were headed next (which also explained the blizzard).... They also found out that there was some kind of restriction or geas on them all that kept them confined to the American West. Lots of plot points were all about the PCs as a group.<br /> <br /> 4th game: easy.... setting was Iraq during the war. They were all military personnel and associated contractors that got put together into a specialized unit. The military characters were invested in being in the military, so they were following their orders. The contractors stayed b/c the group was doing the stuff they were interested in. <br /> <br /> 5th game (current): the band members were independently approached by a corporation and offered very lucrative positions in a division within the company. Sorta Faustian. They were definitely enticed with things their characters wanted. They are the least nice Scions we've ever had and they were okay with the situation. Though, now, at demigod, they are FINALLY starting to question what is going on....<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T10:32:39-07:00","id":289710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289630#post289630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is a concern. It has no solution, aside from re-writing the game. Epics are more useful, more powerful, provide more benefit and generally are cooler. The best Hero Boons are the Immunity Boons, Animal Aspect at Animal 3, and the ability to fly at Sky 2. Aside from those, you're going to notice that Boons just kinda suck. But don't worry, the entire Scion system is terrible, so it'll just fit in fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I noticed it too. I don't feel it's going to be <i>too </i>much of a problem, since we always tend to be light in our respect of the rules when they inconvinience us. I'm confident that I can remove and/or change anything that cause problems, but as long as everyone walks away from the table having had a good time, then everything is just fine.<br /> <br /> As for Boons, after searching a bit I found a pdf with the resources of the old GothamByNight site, which includes their custom boons and purviews. At a first glance they all seem solid, and if anything they are at least way more interesting and cool than the Boons in Hero.<br /> I'm thinking of letting them in my game on a case by case basis, changed if necessary.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 10-22-2014, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T10:38:29-07:00","id":289713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289673#post289673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -snip helpful stuff-<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It does, thanks a lot. I particulary really like the 3rd one, although if I ran something along those lines I would probably change it a bit, since from the sound of it was a very combat-heavy game, and I'd like to give the less combat focused characters a chance to shine right from the start.<br /> <br /> Handwaving the reason their Band was formed is always a possibility, one that may be even interesting to explore in game: why <i>do </i>the PC's stay togheter? Maybe for some reason none of them remember their first meeting, or how they became a group, and they only share the feeling that they belong with each other?<br /> <br /> Edit: Gaaah! I wanted to answer you both in a single post, but for some reasons I couldn't quote both of you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","user":"BlueBiscuit","date":". 10-22-2014, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T10:53:58-07:00","id":289720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289713#post289713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It does, thanks a lot. I particulary really like the 3rd one, although if I ran something along those lines I would probably change it a bit, since from the sound of it was a very combat-heavy game, and I'd like to give the less combat focused characters a chance to shine right from the start.<br /> <br /> Handwaving the reason their Band was formed is always a possibility, one that may be even interesting to explore in game: why <i>do </i>the PC's stay togheter? Maybe for some reason none of them remember their first meeting, or how they became a group, and they only share the feeling that they belong with each other?<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>It was a combat heavy, gruesome beginning, but it didn't stay that way. Though, something you WILL find out.... Scion is designed to be pretty combat heavy. Everything else is pretty vague and you WILL have to do a lot of handwaving to make social characters not useless or over-useful. And a LOT MORE handwaving to making mental characters useful at all. And even the combat stuff falls down around demigod. Also, no decent monsters for them to fight. They don't seem to be made up to face the sort of characters the game generates. Be warned.<br /> <br /> If your group is good with a really vague reason to stay together, those might work. That means that they will largely be chucking all those great backstories as, whatever that was all about, they aren't going to be doing that anymore. Which means the PLAYERS need to know that their backstory and current situation was all flavor text. Otherwise, with a group of diehard roleplayers who invest as much in character creation as your characters do, they are going to be weighing &quot;this nagging feeling I should stay with this guy&quot; against 'staying with these people means giving up everything important to me&quot; or &quot;it's more important to me to stay with these guys then try to get my life back&quot; (with the memory loss thing). The memory loss worked okay for us b/c one character was a 14 yr old outcast type (spooky swap girl), another was effectively Paris Hilton (missing time? like when I got drunk last week?), another was an NFL player who had lost his hearing and with it his job (Thor's thunder can be LOUD when you are right in the middle of it). The other guy was a low level exec who hated his job and had no problem never going back....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 10-22-2014, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T12:20:06-07:00","id":289872,"title":"","content":"It's not like my players would mind if the reason they stay together is a little flimsy, like I said, that's actually kind of the norm in our games. It's just that I'd like for once if our party of PC's was maybe a bit more than the usual &quot;we met at a random taver by chance, decided to go do stuff together&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T16:36:52-07:00","id":290098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289872#post289872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not like my players would mind if the reason they stay together is a little flimsy, like I said, that's actually kind of the norm in our games. It's just that I'd like for once if our party of PC's was maybe a bit more than the usual &quot;we met at a random taver by chance, decided to go do stuff together&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll follow Ajax's example and list off my starts.<br /> <br /> 1) The characters were sent to a &quot;Super Secret&quot; Company that was designed to &quot;keep the peace&quot; between all the pantheons ... and give budding Scions something to do so they didn't cause havoc. This was my first ever Scion game run so it was very &quot;go here for random hookup&quot; but it worked.<br /> <br /> 2) They were all recruited as slaves aboard a ship only to realize they were essentially undead and needed to return to the living.<br /> <br /> 3) Three of the group knew eachother and were recruited by the fourth's parent to get them out of a city. Naturally, this is when Apep devours the sun.<br /> <br /> 4) My current game: The Scions were accused of a crime and Fateful Aura placed them all on the same prison transport bus which is then attacked by government black cars.<br /> <br /> One BIG thing to remember is Fateful Aura. It is your best best best friend as an ST and once you embrace it's potential for sheer happenstance and probability wackiness, the happier you'll be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","user":"Aynie","date":"Quote system start working please 10-22-2014, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T10:42:59-07:00","id":290656,"title":"","content":"Thank you both, those have been incredibly helpful, and now, after having talked with my players, I've started drawing our the a rough outline for the first few sessions. I'll make a proper post about it later.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I was wondering, does a Scion ST screen exist? At least a custom made one? My google fu revealed to me that there was a fan made quick reference sheet, but all links that I've found have gone the way of the dodo. I could make one for print myself, but I feel too lazy to do it if someone out there has already done all the work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T12:21:51-07:00","id":290713,"title":"","content":"There was a French one....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T13:24:45-07:00","id":290746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=290713#post290713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a French one....</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, I do read and speak french, but I would still translate it to English or Italian, for ease of use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T19:09:49-07:00","id":290939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/94027/Scion--cran-du-Conteur\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/2776/94027.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/94027/Scion--cran-du-Conteur\" target=\"_blank\"> Scion : &Eacute;cran du Conteur - Bibliotheque Interdite | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/94027/Scion--cran-du-Conteur\" target=\"_blank\"> http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/94027/Scion--cran-du-Conteur </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Scion : &Eacute;cran du Conteur - Affrontez le DestinLes dieux gaulois sortent de leur retraite pour se joindre &agrave; la lutte contre les Titans.Les h&eacute;ros d </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> but that's not the actual physical thing.... so you'd have to buy it, translate it then spend some quality arts and crafts time... might be easier to just make up one yourself....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T04:32:25-07:00","id":293625,"title":"","content":"So, while working on the Screen and the first session of the game (I'm going to use an adapted version of Of Shadows Yet to Come), I've started to look into enemies and encounter building. I've seen in a lot of old thread that many enemies, as written in the books, are little more than speedbumps, so I was wondering what goes into proper encounter design for Scion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T09:22:32-07:00","id":293775,"title":"","content":"Do you have Scion:Companion? They have a section about creating Titanspawn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:04:08-07:00","id":293915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=293775#post293775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have Scion:Companion? They have a section about creating Titanspawn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I read through it, and I don't remember seeing Titanspawn creation rules, just stuff to help upgrade characters at chargen to demigod or god level, or something along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T12:22:03-07:00","id":294008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=293915#post293915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really? I read through it, and I don't remember seeing Titanspawn creation rules, just stuff to help upgrade characters at chargen to demigod or god level, or something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're thinking of the second section, I believe.It was in the fourth section, which they seem to have used as a kind of grab-bag for everything they could not throw into the other sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T12:39:18-07:00","id":294044,"title":"","content":"Now that you point it out it's true, chapter four is full of random stuff. I personally just forgot about the design titanspaws, pantheons and stuff and went directly to the story hooks and relics bits, which where what immediately interested me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while the information in it is pretty useful in monster design, I find it lacking when it comes to encounter design. It just says &quot;pick a power level&quot; rather vaguely, but doesn't give any clear guide lines to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:01:52-07:00","id":294060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=294044#post294044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that you point it out it's true, chapter four is full of random stuff. I personally just forgot about the design titanspaws, pantheons and stuff and went directly to the story hooks and relics bits, which where what immediately interested me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, while the information in it is pretty useful in monster design, I find it lacking when it comes to encounter design. It just says &amp;quot;pick a power level&amp;quot; rather vaguely, but doesn't give any clear guide lines to that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, I'm still getting used to the rules, so I cannot help you there. Best of luck, and Godspeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:23:25-07:00","id":294081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=294060#post294060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, I'm still getting used to the rules, so I cannot help you there. Best of luck, and Godspeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, and good luck to you as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:44:38-07:00","id":294099,"title":"","content":"For my first game as a Scion ST I put my player in a shady hospital waking up missing piece of their body. After that they more or less stayed together.<br /> <br /> The most interesting monster are the monster you design yourself, special ability and tricky power make for the more memorable encounter. Don't bother with rules, your player have to feel the need to use their power and their brain and not just toss bag of dice. I usually use antagonist for new idea on monster, new look or pantheon oriented opponent and then remake their power to be more interesting in combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2799-astoril","name":"Astoril","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:47:56-07:00","id":294167,"title":"","content":"My problem isn't with coming up with ideas for opponents to throw at my players to test their might against, it's just that given that I don't have fully digested the system yet, neither played an actual session, I'm afraid I may miscalculate the toughness of whatever monster/npc/other stuff I make, relative to my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:49:52-07:00","id":294221,"title":"","content":"If you've got a band of 4, for instance, and you plan on having a full-band encounter, make it so the creature's legend rating and attributes won't immediately kill the players. So if they're all legend 2, maybe make it so the creature is legend 3 or 4, but not with more than 2 epics in any physical attributes. Always keep in mind the number of players that should be taking on the beast.<br /> <br /> And, of course, if you notice a situation is brewing where less than all of them are headed for the encounter, adjust accordingly, or have obstacles in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2775-varygoode","name":"varygoode","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T09:48:13-07:00","id":294945,"title":"","content":"Be very very careful. If you have characters that do not all have at least a secondary focus in combat, anything you put in to challenge the warrior-type will mop the floor with them (with a blood squeegie). However, if you do not make the combat antagonist a challenge to the best warriors, expect for the fight to be o over in10-20 seconds/ticks. If that long...<br /> <br /> And, no, there is no real way to resolve that situation within RAW. It's not as pronounced at Legend 2 as it is at Legend 3 . By Legend 4 it's a real issue and explodes from then on. So suggest your social and mental characters get maxed out stamina-wise (I'm gonna be the goddess of romantic love and cockroaches!) or expect them to end the Big Fight before it starts with their smarts or wiles. Just out of self-preservation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T10:58:36-07:00","id":296006,"title":"","content":"When I run any Scion or Exalted game I use a spreadsheet to figure out challenges. Here's one I've used for Scion.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/scion/miscellaneous/challenges.xml\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/scion/miscellaneous/challenges.x</a>ls<br /> <br /> The first four columns are PCs. The columns after that are familiars or allies.This one is a special case because Dr. Juan's player didn't usually show up for games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":829,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","user":"James McMurray","date":". 10-30-2014, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-29T12:49:06-07:00","id":296078,"title":"","content":"Thanks, those are really useful, though the first link is broken for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-30T12:11:31-07:00","id":297329,"title":"","content":"I tried editing it and things just got crazier. Here'e the URL: <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/scion/miscellaneous/challenges.xls\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/scion/miscellaneous/challenges.xls</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T01:18:45-08:00","id":300863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James McMurray</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=297329#post297329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tried editing it and things just got crazier. Here'e the URL: <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/scion/miscellaneous/challenges.xls\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/scion/miscellaneous/challenges.xls</a></div> </div> </div> </div>That is incredibly helpful, and you sir, are awesome. Thanks a bunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T10:21:18-08:00","id":301261,"title":"","content":"Well Scion takes place in a different universe from WoD (not, that you can't make them cross over). But Scion is pretty much a super hero game with beings from divine mythology. Most super heroes tend to be flashy and public about what they do, as are their villains. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I was doing some research on the nature of Fate binds, and something mentioned that if a Scion pretended to be an ordinary human, then Fate might decide to have a dragon attack them at school. I imagine that would be pretty difficult to hide! Besides, the Scions gain their power from Legend. In order to gain Legend, they need to be well known. Their powers will never grow if they try to hide from the public eye.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Remember, Titan Spawn are otherworldly beings. They do not think the same way mortals do, and they decide to wage <i>war on the Gods</i>! What do they care if mortals discover them, what could they possibly do against their forces?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-03-2014, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T10:57:14-08:00","id":301303,"title":"","content":"If you're looking for them to have a reason to group up, how about something like this?<br /> <br /> <br /> The kitty burglar works her technique to gain access to a designated target. The assassin follows her in and eliminates the target while she starts looting the place of valuables. The Bouncer functions as a look out or security guard, making sure nobody comes to disturb them until the job is done.<br /> <br /> All three of them work together to pull off the mission. ^_^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T12:59:07-08:00","id":301448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=301261#post301261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was doing some research on the nature of Fate binds, and something mentioned that if a Scion pretended to be an ordinary human, then Fate might decide to have a dragon attack them at school. I imagine that would be pretty difficult to hide! Besides, the Scions gain their power from Legend. In order to gain Legend, they need to be well known. Their powers will never grow if they try to hide from the public eye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fateful Aura works with the Legendary Power a Scion has, so a Legend 4-5 Scion trying to not cause trouble will have a dragon show up. A Legend 2-3 scion hiding at a school might find out that the die-hard party kids planning the senior prom are actually Satyrs looking to indoctrinate new kids for their Maenead cult.<br /> <br /> The challenges have to be tough but fair to a Scion's Legend. A social scion hiding out isn't going to really have dragons chasing her, but she will encounter troubles that will require her to probably rely on her own social powers to get through them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T14:16:18-08:00","id":301524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=301448#post301448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fateful Aura works with the Legendary Power a Scion has, so a Legend 4-5 Scion trying to not cause trouble will have a dragon show up. A Legend 2-3 scion hiding at a school might find out that the die-hard party kids planning the senior prom are actually Satyrs looking to indoctrinate new kids for their Maenead cult.<br /> <br /> The challenges have to be tough but fair to a Scion's Legend. A social scion hiding out isn't going to really have dragons chasing her, but she will encounter troubles that will require her to probably rely on her own social powers to get through them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmm, I'm not too knowledgeable about Maenads aside from True Blood. What's so bad about joining one of their cults? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Oh right, the meat statue sacrifice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-03-2014, 05:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T17:47:01-08:00","id":301623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=301524#post301524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hmmm, I'm not too knowledgeable about Maenads aside from True Blood. What's so bad about joining one of their cults? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Oh right, the meat statue sacrifice.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're psychotic Dionysus worshipers most famous for tearing a man limb from limb. Also, the leader of those Maenads was his own mother. So yeah, they aren't exactly nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T19:29:10-08:00","id":301696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=301623#post301623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, the leader of those Maenads was his own mother.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wha... how? What the?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T19:54:16-08:00","id":301705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=301696#post301696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wha... how? What the?</div> </div> </div> </div>King banned worshiping Dionysus(because he was his cousin before he became a god), so he lured the king into a dark wood and whipped the local Maenads, including the king's mother, into a murderous frenzy, causing them to rip him apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T23:11:39-08:00","id":301844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=301705#post301705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">King banned worshiping Dionysus(because he was his cousin before he became a god), so he lured the king into a dark wood and whipped the local Maenads, including the king's mother, into a murderous frenzy, causing them to rip him apart.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wait, I misinterpreted the words. I thought you said he had given birth to himself. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T23:42:56-08:00","id":301890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilmarmelade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=289440#post289440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as with many other WoD games, you might want to ask your players about the subjects they consider taboo. It's a game about ancient mythology, and sometimes it was not pretty. There's a lot a myths that features rape, slavery, bestiality, sometimes even pedophilia...<br /> Also, with the right powers, it's super easy for Scions to brainwash people, which can make some players uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, I may sound a bit prudish, but clearly establishing which subjects are okay to use and which ones aren't helps a lot in having a healthy table.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I say if you're going to play a game based on mythology, you should go all out. Crazy f**ked up shit is part of the charm. Your PC's may not have to participate in such activities (they're from the modern age, after all), but that doesn't mean you shouldn't toss in a villain or two who thinks the old ways are best. Its Disney censorship that turned Hades into Satan, and Zeus into some benevolent deity.<br /> <br /> In my game, Hades would be a perfect gentleman, and Zeus would be sticking himself in every woman that came within arm's reach! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T07:11:42-08:00","id":302123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=301890#post301890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I say if you're going to play a game based on mythology, you should go all out. Crazy f**ked up shit is part of the charm. Your PC's may not have to participate in such activities (they're from the modern age, after all), but that doesn't mean you shouldn't toss in a villain or two who thinks the old ways are best. Its Disney censorship that turned Hades into Satan, and Zeus into some benevolent deity.<br /> <br /> In my game, Hades would be a perfect gentleman, and Zeus would be sticking himself in every woman that came within arm's reach! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know you're going for silliness, but while mythology is horrific and filled with a lack of regard for anything (usually anything female) it's not a bad thing to make sure your players are going to be ok with subjects being thrown at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T07:51:30-08:00","id":302171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aynie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=302123#post302123\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I know you're going for silliness, but while mythology is horrific and filled with a lack of regard for anything (usually anything female) it's not a bad thing to make sure your players are going to be ok with subjects being thrown at them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. Remember, the game's only fun if everyone is having fun(unless they're not having fun because they want to kill the other player characters or something like that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T10:19:23-08:00","id":302424,"title":"","content":"On other news, I'm mostly done with my custom ST screen, and I was wondering if anyone knew any good piece of art I could put outside of it for my players to look at while I scheme behind the screen? I was thinking of just printing out the covers of the books, but I'd love some variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-23T11:52:06-08:00","id":320096,"title":"","content":"Well then, the first two sessions of the game recently happened, and overall I have to say I was pleased by the results, and my players all had fun. I have to thank everyone here who gave me suggestions on how to start a Story, they turned out to be really useful.<br /> <br /> I ran my players through a heavily modified version of Of Shadows Yet To Come, and they have recently arrived at the destination Fate pushed them towards: Emerald City. (If that sounds familiar to you, it's because it's from Mutant &amp; Masterminds. I really like it, and never got to use it, and really, Scion is pretty much a supers game).<br /> Next few sessions I plan to introduce a few NPC's, and start those character plots that I have all figured out, and at least start seeding the others, with some cooperation with the players.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, the house rules I have in play seemed to work fine, though it when it came down to the encounter with the Oni, I felt the characters had trouble overcoming his soak, though that may have been just unlucky rolls on damage.<br /> Has anyone ever felt this problem, with the enemies as statted in the books?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T09:19:51-08:00","id":320795,"title":"","content":"Even for a starting Scion at, say, Legend 3, high Str and epic Str + high Brawl + Crushing Grip Knack doing Agg in a Clinch almost always equals one dead oni in very short order. The head just pops off like a bottle top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T11:57:46-08:00","id":320964,"title":"","content":"Really? Ours was just beaten on the head repeatedly with the motorcycle of one of the PC's, and then run through with the telephone pole he had thrown at them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T13:58:05-08:00","id":321046,"title":"","content":"Now, onto character plots, the one I've mostly figured out is for Anastasia, the Scion of Loki.<br /> My idea was to introduce to her Sigyn, Loki's wife, as wanting use the PC, one of the few children of her husband that aren't dead, loyal to the Titans or complete puppets in his hands, as a way to both prevent Ragnarock and save Loki's life. The trickester himself, however, has his own designs to survive the Doom of the Aesir, and will try to manipulate Anastasia (and her Band). The idea would be to have Sygin tell the PC that there exist a ritual that would finally bind mistletoe to not harm Baldr. I'm unsure on what this ritual would actually entail, however, so I'm open to suggestions, if anyone is willing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-24T16:05:48-08:00","id":321137,"title":"","content":"The Ragnarok book mentions blood, song, and runes as all reoccurring elements in Norse magic. Including these three in copious amounts seems like a good start. Mistilteinn(lit meaning: Mistletoe) also seems useful, considering it was suppose to kill Baldur in some ...interesting variant myths. Maybe destroying it as part of the ritual(at least, that's what Loki might TELL her).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T03:23:06-08:00","id":321615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=321137#post321137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ragnarok book mentions blood, song, and runes as all reoccurring elements in Norse magic. Including these three in copious amounts seems like a good start. Mistilteinn(lit meaning: Mistletoe) also seems useful, considering it was suppose to kill Baldur in some ...interesting variant myths. Maybe destroying it as part of the ritual(at least, that's what Loki might TELL her).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I don't have the Ragnarok book, so I didn't know that. Hmm, blood, song and runes... Looking through wikipedia, I've found that mistletoe was used by druids in rituals, and that originally Mistilteinn was guarded by a King turned Draugr. Man, that just gives me Skyrim flashbacks.<br /> <br /> My thoughts: Fate says that Baldur will die slain by Mistletoe. This could either be the spear forged by Loki with the plant, or the Sword of the Undead king Prain. So Anastasia's quest is twofold: complete the binding of Baldur's invulnerability with the Mistletoe, and recover and Mistletinn (and then perhaps bind the sword to not harm Baldr? Destroy it? Reforge it and change it's name and nature?).<br /> For the first step in her mission my idea is to have Sigyn point her toward a hidden cult of druid, who guard a sacred divine oak tree, on which grows a descendant of the same Mistletoe that Frigg had overlooked. She will have to persuade them to let her perform the ritual to pluck the mistletoe, the first component of the ritual spell.<br /> <br /> As for the druids, I'm thinking to have them be something more than humans: shapeshifters, perhaps werewolves or werebears, or even a mix, and depending on her actions, Anastasia may gain one or more of them as Followers.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T09:40:14-08:00","id":321887,"title":"","content":"Won't Loki be pissed at her for undermining his plans? Won't he already have figured out what she was doing and stopped it? Is he playing a deeper game? If Loki is not bound and she is not 100% busy keeping serpent venom from dripping on him, why isn't Narfi still alive? How does she feel about the &quot;other woman&quot; Angrboda and her 3 kids? About Sleipnir? That might inform how she feels about yet another by-blow of her husband... Considering the precedents in a lot of Norse and Germanic mythology, wouldn't Sigyn be trying to advocate for pride of place for her sons over those other, less legitimate kids of Loki? Especially if she knows the prophecies of Ragnarok. I'm sure she would prefer to not have her husband tied to a rock with her sons guts and change over to a full-time home caregiver/earthquake preventer....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T11:27:58-08:00","id":322002,"title":"","content":"As I understand it, I thought that Loki is going to be bound with his Narfi's guts only after Baldr's death by mitletoe? As for his interfering, I believe Hero says most of the time he's watched personally by either Odin or Thor, and his ability to act is limited to mostly limited means? I envision Loki would try to have the ritual changed so that the fate of Baldr's killer is passed over to someone else, perhaps even the PC, or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> As for Sygin, I hadn't thought about it, but now that you mention it, perhaps her motivation is to have her children rescued from their fates, and the PC is just the most convenient tool? Perhaps once the doom of Loki is averted, she'll cut loose Anastasia from her support, and become an opponent. I imagine that part of the labour may include turning back Nari from wolf to human.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/138-bluebiscuit","name":"BlueBiscuit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T12:52:30-08:00","id":322085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=322002#post322002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, I thought that Loki is going to be bound with his Narfi's guts only after Baldr's death by mitletoe? As for his interfering, I believe Hero says most of the time he's watched personally by either Odin or Thor, and his ability to act is limited to mostly limited means? I envision Loki would try to have the ritual changed so that the fate of Baldr's killer is passed over to someone else, perhaps even the PC, or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> As for Sygin, I hadn't thought about it, but now that you mention it, perhaps her motivation is to have her children rescued from their fates, and the PC is just the most convenient tool? Perhaps once the doom of Loki is averted, she'll cut loose Anastasia from her support, and become an opponent. I imagine that part of the labour may include turning back Nari from wolf to human.</div> </div> </div> </div> To be fair, Loki may be responsible for Baldur dying, but not for him staying dead. Wouldn't it be easier or everyone if the two roles (and their punishment) be wrapped up in one neat little package...<br /> <br /> Also, maybe he might just approach them straight up. Golden Boy's fated to die, he'll reason, and Loki doesn't want to do it. Wouldn't it be better to pin the fate(and the horrible after-efects) on someone who isn't on the side of the World?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-01T09:51:34-08:00","id":327144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BlueBiscuit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/285045-new-scion-st-asking-questions?p=322002#post322002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand it, I thought that Loki is going to be bound with his Narfi's guts only after Baldr's death by mitletoe? As for his interfering, I believe Hero says most of the time he's watched personally by either Odin or Thor, and his ability to act is limited to mostly limited means? I envision Loki would try to have the ritual changed so that the fate of Baldr's killer is passed over to someone else, perhaps even the PC, or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> As for Sygin, I hadn't thought about it, but now that you mention it, perhaps her motivation is to have her children rescued from their fates, and the PC is just the most convenient tool? Perhaps once the doom of Loki is averted, she'll cut loose Anastasia from her support, and become an opponent. I imagine that part of the labour may include turning back Nari from wolf to human.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Scion there is a very deep thread of the Norse gods are all about avoiding their Fate (contrasting to the actual Norse gods just dealing with it and moving forward being themselves...). Either way, there is more than an implication that everyone KNOWS what their fates are going to be. So, if you are a mom, you have a complete dick of a philandering husband who doesn't seem very interested in your mutual children and the eventual, known fate of said sons is completely and utterly horrific, what's a mother to do? Even if Loki's known dickishness is mostly future tense, does that really affect your thinking if you're Sigyn? I would be doing EVERYTHING in my power to try to get this half-mortal nothing in a position where it could be him and not Narfi or her and not me that's going to get the raw, pointy end of the Fate-stick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}